10	82c803b3-4019-40d4-9865-63c45a7d650a	\N	9	11	auth-cert.html	html	\N	\N	20.12. Certificate Authentication#	\N	\N	\N	\N	20.12. Certificate Authentication#	\N	\N	\N	\N	18	en	{"title": "20.12. Certificate Authentication#", "filename": "auth-cert.html", "chunk_count": 1, "chunk_index": 0}	Page: 20.12. Certificate Authentication#\nSource: auth-cert.html\n\n20.12. Certificate Authentication\n#\nThis authentication method uses SSL client certificates to perform authentication. It is therefore only available for SSL connections; see\nSection 18.9.2\nfor SSL configuration instructions. When using this authentication method, the server will require that the client provide a valid, trusted certificate. No password prompt will be sent to the client. The\ncn\n(Common Name) attribute of the certificate will be compared to the requested database user name, and if they match the login will be allowed. User name mapping can be used to allow\ncn\nto be different from the database user name.\nThe following configuration options are supported for SSL certificate authentication:\nmap\nAllows for mapping between system and database user names. See\nSection 20.2\nfor details.\nIt is redundant to use the\nclientcert\noption with\ncert\nauthentication because\ncert\nauthentication is effectively\ntrust\nauthentication with\nclientcert=verify-full\n.	150305d739292ccaac272122db0daaf25817380622409839b33e70af308804f3	\N	0	1	bge-base-en-v1.5	[0.2215529,0.9058702,-2.8230677,-0.48422545,1.2711211,-0.13852626,0.5720894,0.7516209,0.51870304,-0.6562916,-1.2249455,0.2505376,0.9246944,-1.1353012,0.49226803,-0.58031493,-0.3906099,-1.1364474,0.13553141,-0.5827113,-0.8572723,-1.0421355,-0.08686123,-0.17237371,1.1871657,0.47828117,-0.10368471,0.932249,-1.3307027,-0.7685558,0.18764415,0.3907071,1.7330319,-0.13524729,-0.25230348,-0.7772113,-0.04448277,0.31313476,-0.35568187,0.5494668,1.7051796,0.20149449,0.41570666,-0.110336885,0.084028445,0.89393324,0.24915954,0.67907774,1.5983417,-0.095752284,-0.09927168