286	67831603-7487-4238-88eb-7ee168495086	\N	285	287	high-availability.html	html	\N	\N	Chapter 26. High Availability, Load Balancing, and Replication	\N	\N	\N	\N	Chapter 26. High Availability, Load Balancing, and Replication	\N	\N	\N	\N	18	en	{"title": "Chapter 26. High Availability, Load Balancing, and Replication", "filename": "high-availability.html", "chunk_count": 2, "chunk_index": 1}	Page: Chapter 26. High Availability, Load Balancing, and Replication\nSource: high-availability.html\n\nSolutions can also be categorized by their granularity. Some solutions can deal only with an entire database server, while others allow control at the per-table or per-database level.\nPerformance must be considered in any choice. There is usually a trade-off between functionality and performance. For example, a fully synchronous solution over a slow network might cut performance by more than half, while an asynchronous one might have a minimal performance impact.\nThe remainder of this section outlines various failover, replication, and load balancing solutions.	685ad55d5e13f3374ca88f65c688429a1d4707c587e7211e1651f34c61905650	\N	1	2	bge-base-en-v1.5	[0.17795289,1.4977312,-3.8723412,-0.5110072,1.8147907,-0.91941214,0.4836445,0.044479188,0.24175467,-0.45192832,-0.31889352,-0.058251042,0.9872925,0.5962749,-0.44120744,0.09271212,-0.17942692,-0.7737124,-0.23928441,0.6813611,-0.18367825,-0.3087367,-0.42368114,-0.496348,0.39269277,1.048627,-0.81032616,0.13249293,-1.0199662,0.18939671,-0.16045159,-0.6728906,0.5094419,-1.1170162,-0.92978525,0.11102014,-0.26695466,-0.41015047,0.22739165,0.50486916,0.46403986,-0.49750873,0.584208,-1.4878076,0.78815687,-0.17723015,0.58913636,0.98935336,1.3744613,-1.8892394,0.65535706,-0.19709426,0.41046026,-0.80039835,1.0219601,0.6324489,-0.89808,1.2470415,-0.3672335,-1.1367223,1.7698898,0.94653064,-0.37727526,1.1028947,0.51777375,-0.13799836,-0.72902256,0.85653806,0.08156438,-1.3746562,0.75503445,-0.3344255,-0.38590634,0.05649262,-0.22241206,-0.13493556,-0