506	8b97ebfb-7eb9-4a6a-8b2c-fb67bb31304d	\N	505	507	logical-replication-quick-setup.html	html	\N	\N	29.14. Quick Setup#	\N	\N	\N	\N	29.14. Quick Setup#	\N	\N	\N	\N	18	en	{"title": "29.14. Quick Setup#", "filename": "logical-replication-quick-setup.html", "chunk_count": 1, "chunk_index": 0}	Page: 29.14. Quick Setup#\nSource: logical-replication-quick-setup.html\n\n29.14. Quick Setup\n#\nFirst set the configuration options in\npostgresql.conf\n:\nwal_level = logical\nThe other required settings have default values that are sufficient for a basic setup.\npg_hba.conf\nneeds to be adjusted to allow replication (the values here depend on your actual network configuration and user you want to use for connecting):\nhost     all     repuser     0.0.0.0/0     scram-sha-256\nThen on the publisher database:\nCREATE PUBLICATION mypub FOR TABLE users, departments;\nAnd on the subscriber database:\nCREATE SUBSCRIPTION mysub CONNECTION 'dbname=foo host=bar user=repuser' PUBLICATION mypub;\nThe above will start the replication process, which synchronizes the initial table contents of the tables\nusers\nand\ndepartments\nand then starts replicating incremental changes to those tables.	c6dc62b322f98a13bc9460ab970f43820fb20e863459150cc5f1fee42f4de70d	\N	0	1	bge-base-en-v1.5	[0.46701568,1.8055491,-3.6041198,-1.2350036,0.7502706,-0.87580234,0.43734935,0.6550148,-0.5942513,-0.78052574,-0.38126403,0.5298682,0.08998579,-0.10330478,-0.6159895,-0.09162508,0.31042945,-0.66359925,-0.1802324,0.64289385,-0.79251343,-0.7883862,-0.6368599,-0.91676325,1.1527796,1.0176079,-0.6710827,0.07303962,-0.38024208,0.10113571,0.13368759,0.29331857,-0.15523444,-0.9926644,-0.12431127,-1.1872668,-0.03706283,0.03917335,0.07422332,0.059313644,-0.17836957,0.25687328,0.25576955,-1.3096038,-0.35629243,-0.16156352,1.55811,-0.34040338,1.56561,-1.7404176,-0.4369059,-0.016632251,0.40347993,-0.9978775,1.1589166,1.2826291,-0.33138627,1.4125277,0.27102897,-0.8682466,2.0700388,0.47392854,-0.3891305,1.705972,-0.3059857,0.02031