539	6fcf018c-e647-4370-acd0-8428c982a6fa	\N	538	540	manage-ag-tablespaces.html	html	\N	\N	22.6. Tablespaces#	\N	\N	\N	\N	22.6. Tablespaces#	\N	\N	\N	\N	18	en	{"title": "22.6. Tablespaces#", "filename": "manage-ag-tablespaces.html", "chunk_count": 3, "chunk_index": 2}	Page: 22.6. Tablespaces#\nSource: manage-ag-tablespaces.html\n\nOnce created, a tablespace can be used from any database, provided the requesting user has sufficient privilege. This means that a tablespace cannot be dropped until all objects in all databases using the tablespace have been removed.\nTo remove an empty tablespace, use the\nDROP TABLESPACE\ncommand.\nTo determine the set of existing tablespaces, examine the\npg_tablespace\nsystem catalog, for example\nSELECT spcname, spcowner::regrole, pg_tablespace_location(oid) FROM pg_tablespace;\nIt is possible to find which databases use which tablespaces; see\nTable 9.76\n. The\npsql\nprogram's\n\\db\nmeta-command is also useful for listing the existing tablespaces.\nThe directory\n$PGDATA/pg_tblspc\ncontains symbolic links that point to each of the non-built-in tablespaces defined in the cluster. Although not recommended, it is possible to adjust the tablespace layout by hand by redefining these links. Under no circumstances perform this operation while the server is running.	3174982a0d4679898088c50686498dd14ffabbebac819416d5e9b746519e2a28	\N	2	3	bge-base-en-v1.5	[0.24076013,1.4401945,-2.3508732,-1.4137677,0.07094869,-0.6592748,0.24012972,0.29507285,0.22170043,-0.79567367,0.043147895,-0.42430294,1.2466798,0.08918765,-0.20015022,0.32571042,-0.5806157,-0.41798225,-0.7536311,-0.089246586,0.26595822,-1.478584,-0.09105403,-0.48792696,0.75103694,1.659254,-0.36504462,0.08297143,-0.07335574,0.5451923,0.4535033,1.0841165,-0.44628403,-0.20586056,-0.06367871,-1.1720327,0.9846959,0.46366134,-0.72199756,0.39816773,0.9517234,0.05414603,0.07669807,-1.2584676,-0.1847185,-0.21033253,0.9913771,0.46333483,1.4677817,-0.6948771,-0.16563913,-0.48978248,0.122492924,-1.108