1020	7532322f-4f7a-40b6-a854-f3acd5c3b135	\N	1019	1021	wal-intro.html	html	\N	\N	28.3. Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)#	\N	\N	\N	\N	28.3. Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)#	\N	\N	\N	\N	18	en	{"title": "28.3. Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)#", "filename": "wal-intro.html", "chunk_count": 2, "chunk_index": 1}	Page: 28.3. Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)#\nSource: wal-intro.html\n\n. By archiving the WAL data we can support reverting to any time instant covered by the available WAL data: we simply install a prior physical backup of the database, and replay the WAL just as far as the desired time. What's more, the physical backup doesn't have to be an instantaneous snapshot of the database state — if it is made over some period of time, then replaying the WAL for that period will fix any internal inconsistencies.	b4a53114c1fd60ca40bb05aa8510e19e862fe71ee4a1ff30ae0f73b03c671c09	\N	1	2	bge-base-en-v1.5	[0.93709815,0.38008368,-3.4231741,-1.2833793,0.61999696,-0.58313566,0.6136282,0.08856895,0.56093186,-1.1070455,-0.17304243,0.8757495,1.3178124,0.83690614,-0.5930425,-0.55807847,-0.10903447,-1.1811745,-0.04865552,0.7594638,0.48876253,-0.7802614,-0.52588296,-0.3770923,0.6844192,0.58703274,-0.07856436,1.3246486,-0.9250886,0.5965494,1.8137337,-1.0464672,0.24922392,-0.3997803,-0.2764038,-1.2589267,-0.18850929,-0.99707717,0.32904553,-0.04826862,0.61712724,0.7627217,1.0862358,0.023039207,1.0096073,0.6395914,0.64453274,-0.28407547,0.9490089,-1.3023378,-0.09611517,0.48548043,-0.20475423,-0.5132597,1.1105542,0.2238395,0.2402003,-0.29230478,0.60493416,-1.1476753,1.9688343,0.4630191,9.223968e-06,1.6782938,-0.30908749,-0.6349566,-0.66764873,0.47182968,0.62298894,-1.6592281,1.0218712,1.3516523,-0.8979509,0.31808904,0.69579047,0.53911704,-0.25345218,0.0348611,0.12879704,0.33366352,-0.094167195,0.36683708,0.80099404,-0.17013088,0.71491605,-0.09446028,-0.12109846,0.46201685,-0.9100481,1.5986803,-0.08622188,-0.22540379,1.0557954,0.61658645,-1.2120262,-0.11734951,0.46813774,0.5402081,-1.1631033,-0.06427618,-0.86831135,