24	how can I Sets the maximum number of background processes that the cluster can support ?	To set the maximum number of background processes (worker processes) that the cluster can support, use the following command:\n\n```sql\nALTER SYSTEM SET max_worker_processes TO 'new_value';\n```\n\nReplace `new_value` with the desired number. For example:\n\n```sql\nALTER SYSTEM SET max_worker_processes TO '16';\n```\n\nAfter setting this value, restart PostgreSQL to apply the changes:\n\n```bash\nsudo systemctl restart postgresql\n```	[0.4939874,1.5129396,-3.6184464,-0.43762314,0.77847856,-1.4816799,0.28138494,0.6345425,-0.5088513,-0.27863622,0.16852629,1.0855919,1.4773277,1.0479188,-0.23524891,-0.5749688,-0.8406281,-0.93973994,-0.8849922,-0.6598142,0.2649398,-0.8013702,-0.29000688,0.003163,0.67084885,1.4453475,0.7335141,-0.5960446,-0.08462978,-0.06976853,1.6175854,-0.6677518,-0.6092727,-0.79708266,-0.24028945,-0.6259894,0.7094118,-0.5410998,-0.37401137,0.1861713,0.47548887,-0.6642571,0.09536777,-1.3477345,0.26423773,0.62171674,1.5515198,-0.42927173,1.5373831,-1.4884588,-0.26238838,0.1688456,-0.15929623,-0.35011378,-0.5126552,0.7029463,-0.3616144,0.56628114,0.49113184,-0.017593367,1.3791435,0.54729074,-1.0648679,1.4949106,0.25758916,-0.067934506,-0.67804617,0.92972714,-0.29380983,-0.57149816,0.7535153,-0.3960451,0.015083213,0.7379025,-0.41349107,0.5235053,-0.41786683,-0.38477847,0.33799982,1.2340652,0.29069266,0.41810134,1.4274325,-0.2876789,1.675391,0.7460953,-0.44953495,-0.37325054,-1.3261757,1.8547865,0.44789124,0.25226152,0.18513507,0.24056067,-0.5344747,0.5181281,0.014488156,0.5685074,-1.4164586,-0.43655947,0.39962626,-0.7689263,-0.27925527,-0.7414457,0.08524668,-0.48723903,-0.4934469,0.72131884,0.9946684,-0.007617859,-0.027341299,0.30207527,-0.79864055,-0.16160862,-0.8589791,-1.0625831,0.62301373,0.31639403,-0.08064155,1.1820252,-0.37960866,0.26068366,-0.8870807,-0.45355156,-0.14059345,0.68135506,-1.4338243,0.5990955,0.7118144,-1.9385637,1.2469703,-0.77135223,-0.75934