29	what are the impacts for a vacuum full ?	Performing a `VACUUM FULL` on a PostgreSQL table has several significant impacts:\n\n1. **Disk Space**: It can reclaim more disk space by removing dead rows and compacting the data.\n2. **Performance Impact**: It requires an `ACCESS EXCLUSIVE` lock, preventing any other transactions from accessing the table during the operation.\n3. **Duration**: It is much slower compared to a regular `VACUUM`.\n\nHere’s how you can execute it:\n\n```sql\nVACUUM FULL your_table_name;\n```\n\nReplace `your_table_name` with the actual name of your table.	[1.5973397,1.1331897,-3.9189138,-0.18922113,1.2527351,0.95552295,-0.045024585,0.89230883,0.037301447,-0.8335279,-0.13740888,0.1340902,1.4202895,1.0644292,0.17168587,-0.6538892,-0.35115615,-1.3097396,0.50066024,-0.10305383,-0.6136604,-0.4012824,-1.9593536,-0.304608,0.35880044,1.0767255,1.7635058,0.8770517,0.23704754,0.32419673,0.46660566,1.1079743,-1.6043446,-1.5830331,-1.7146229,-0.23444629,1.0400769,0.43700752,0.66838807,-0.2280975,-0.9150086,-0.5050678,0.109173946,-0.05153282,0.3256842,1.0437989,-0.38929185,-0.36797655,0.30506757,-0.19303845,0.3760288,-2.0094068,-1.4231845,0.13189727,1.8270794,-0.5832665,0.20865358,-0.84208703,1.7021712,-0.18790783,-0.35847166,0.7105334,-0.43950588,1.3289229,0.28385755,-0.9900896,-0.09606681,0.13913104,0.0979582,-1.3741364,0.8326015,-0.32726157,0.7996636,-0.5673288,-0.8071245,0.95167565,-0.5545385,-0.026071357,0.4683286,0.030515037,-0.3241393,-0.014308062,1.7335618,0.24483489,1.6934254,-1.4935294,-0.4821558,-0.016512292,-0.04354286,1.2501069,0.4860659,0.18284255,-0.4296451,0.10320056,-1.1832494,0.26576173,-0.097572915,1.7630244,0.33450684,-0.007551611,-0.32741535,-0.21460313,0.93708235,-0.6098448,0.58976024,-0.7491993,-0.67888,0.24144532,0.7223971,-0.122166395,-0.9717818,0.013239163,-0.67972064,-0.42992687,-0.1237925,-0.6292289,1.6075234,-1.0747238,-0.20228763,1.5246006,0.8925607,-0.14560828,-0.004533929,-0.43934697,-0.88090616,0.069980755,-1.7887769,-0.1