30	how can i configure streaming replication without replication slots?	Configuring streaming replication without using replication slots is not directly possible because replication slots are essential for managing and tracking active standby servers in PostgreSQL. However, you can disable replication slots temporarily or configure them to a minimum value if needed.\n\nTo set up streaming replication with minimal slot configuration:\n\n1. **Primary Server**:\n   - Ensure `max_wal_senders` is set appropriately.\n   - Set `wal_level` to `replica` or `logical`.\n\n2. **Standby Server**:\n   - No need for replication slots if you're not using logical decoding.\n\nHere’s the exact configuration:\n\n```sql\n-- On Primary Server\nALTER SYSTEM SET max_wal_senders TO 3;\nALTER SYSTEM SET wal_level TO replica;\n\n-- Optionally, on Standby Server (if using physical replication)\nRESET max_replication_slots;\n```\n\nIf you need to use logical replication later, ensure proper settings like `max_logical_replication_workers` and `max_replication_slots`.\n\nFor a minimal setup without slots:\n\n```sql\nALTER SYSTEM SET max_wal_senders TO 3; -- Adjust as needed\nALTER SYSTEM SET wal_level TO replica;\nRESET max_replication_slots;\n```\n\nApply the changes with:\n\n```bash\npg_ctl reload\n```	[-0.41241065,1.6780192,-3.8191862,-1.3784891,0.14718837,-1.7371337,0.082896344,1.0971775,-0.8533588,-1.313861,-0.7248516,1.9348596,0.85192883,1.1557522,-1.7534081,0.29541218,-0.3456053,-0.39142075,0.05055281,0.5469506,-0.874185,-1.180139,-0.34436408,-0.5392303,1.3159211,0.5680124,-0.5011474,0.24951652,-0.38994825,0.1961241,1.5843971,0.41355044,0.47734734,-0.45606965,0.7058848,-0.3869818,-0.8599693,-0.5138968,-1.1407746,0.9317482,-0.8330485,-0.3632951,-0.3407431,-0.8352467,0.53857154,-0.09479295,2.4801106,0.1703942,0.25813282,-2.5902944,0.8874241,-0.24594426,-1.0633242,-1.8178626,-0.021871615,0.64364046,-1.3514969,1.5595332,0.93358517,-0.97561705,0.09571143,0.3512209,0.30854708,0.8671251,-0.3301