31	how can i know the replication is active ?	To check if streaming replication is active, you can monitor the `pg_stat_replication` view on the primary server. This view provides details about all connected standby servers.\n\nHere’s how to query it:\n\n```sql\nSELECT * FROM pg_stat_replication;\n```\n\nThis will show you information such as the connection status, applied WAL location, and other relevant metrics for each standby server.\n\nAdditionally, you can check the `pg_replication_slots` view on both primary and standby servers if you are using replication slots:\n\n```sql\n-- On Primary Server\nSELECT * FROM pg_replication_slots;\n\n-- On Standby Server (if configured)\nSELECT * FROM pg_stat_wal_receiver;\n```\n\nThese commands will give you a comprehensive overview of the replication status.	[-0.1174855,-0.3774313,-4.6476207,-1.1657313,1.5192603,-1.8196505,0.5740615,1.0128175,0.6482395,-0.6534114,-1.2168523,1.7312058,1.0634727,0.977097,-1.7760469,-0.78939366,0.7979958,-1.9919217,-0.4835984,0.29653516,0.5082188,-0.3142028,-0.13101806,0.3238628,2.014367,1.7953358,0.07693775,0.43150377,0.6027889,-0.9024698,1.1565471,-0.30359656,-0.1693911,-1.0654114,0.87753445,-0.5559624,0.71788543,0.1402908,0.082380466,-0.020192532,-1.8491799,-0.07053354,0.27822694,-0.3512213,0.71120256,0.11789753,1.1750998,-0.33982918,0.6497699,-1.0665712,-0.46717843,0.091061704,-0.23411895,-0.5309248,0.9460943,0.7226534,-0.58553135,0.9358549,0.12984835,-1.3802189,0.49348024,0.1620682,0.50184137,1.26715,0.21415474,-0.37456635,-0.33142102,1.357945,-0.10839105,-0.81321263,0.44264653,0.013893553,0.37556285,-0.43714523,0.16266634,0.4071513,0.2029819,-0.16342701,-0.30211517,0.33791655,0.012775957,0.25159237,2.489029,-0.30593795,2.1957912,0.8350521,-1.1647254,-0.7981199,-0.71091485,1.0408144,1.7300828,0.06615919,1.2555838,0.15953867,-0.7152027,0.22830954,-0.22715563,0.8404293,-1.043789,0.26871622,-0.44094956,-0.033486698,-1.0933906,-0.2271265,0.11871049,0.71546626,0.028187968,-0.30162522,-0.721658