33	how do i set shared_buffers ?	To configure `shared_buffers` in PostgreSQL 18, you can set it during the server startup or through a configuration file. Here’s how:\n\n### For Startup Command:\n```bash\npostgres -c "shared_buffers=256MB" -D /path/to/data/directory\n```\n\n### In `postgresql.conf` File:\nEdit the `postgresql.conf` file to include:\n```plaintext\nshared_buffers = 256MB\n```\n\nThis sets `shared_buffers` to 256 MB. Adjust the value based on your system's RAM and workload requirements. Typically, a good starting point is around 25-30% of total system memory.	[0.7125633,0.4128218,-2.7945673,-1.7125053,1.2623572,0.12680565,0.51696396,0.47283468,-1.365458,-0.77167106,-1.7506318,0.7459716,0.31433752,1.7262403,-0.012867275,0.8707076,0.051612817,-0.5888717,0.014477348,0.3624555,-0.81982034,-0.22576986,0.13471411,-0.19254214,1.7859176,1.1584698,-0.13644971,0.59298116,-0.79662037,0.48994815,0.54666275,0.17597716,-0.31502306,-0.50475276,1.2166107,-0.6056878,-0.5776417,-0.9849446,-1.1280141,0.2667634,-0.32110947,0.47432032,0.7726713,-1.1603055,-0.15800864,0.041899063,1.1883165,0.7856213,1.2904397,-0.6064364,-0.20531149,-0.24230051,-0.8075216,-2.4018056,1.389759,-0.14917433,-0.4796035,1.305878,0.5399334,-1.2854269,1.3896968,0.67880374,0.45244065,0.69040114,0.7231275,1.6535641,-0.3432171,1.0451733,-0.06542582,-0.0027242193,-0.15700334,1.1463785,0.94460815,-0.29414836,0.44605875,0.042607535,-0.8449525,-0.05313052,-0.7414186,0.64003855,-0.029488564,0.8352225,1.3393964,-0.02304039,1.1425774,0.4959551,-0.16847387,-0.6238203,-0.87478375,1.5577645,-0.53107905,0.31630316,0.50474966,1.0952579,0.33407596,-0.17218406,-0.16073963,0.2981124,-0.062396333,-0.14463991,-0.6298279,0.41780406,1.1671062,-0.2188686,-0.024984084,-0.05944467,-0.0886264,0.4429375,0.5889496,0.42864677,-0.53352827,-0.18610248,0.5740416,-0.2056157,0.97770095,-0.8395922,1.3428774,-0.09994655,-0.39511326,0.69363123,-0.5804646,-0.41980574,0.51507866,0.67026186,0.14724937,0.08341435,-1.0009106,0.27786177,0.47