36	how can i know the number of active sessions ?	To determine the number of active sessions, you can query the `pg_stat_activity` system view. Here is the SQL command:\n\n```sql\nSELECT count(*) FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE state != 'idle';\n```\n\nThis query counts the number of sessions that are not in an idle state, indicating active sessions.	[-0.5217267,0.13964106,-4.1395583,-1.0701135,0.9039173,-1.8739699,1.6510596,-0.36671865,0.5707679,-0.5279271,-0.794439,0.0039834767,1.0881943,0.61083233,-0.32811716,-1.6656446,-0.4181843,-1.5675098,-0.8493324,-0.781828,0.45056894,-0.57581645,0.16946776,-0.09230199,2.236254,1.9776644,-0.043555647,0.37104276,0.112784535,0.23230213,0.68374234,-1.1464704,0.28977677,0.523135,-0.38822985,-0.7297771,0.68703264,0.17819719,-0.110943,0.010411188,-0.06528256,-0.72649646,0.056505296,-0.1581098,-0.3768725,-1.2637415,0.3618038,0.45602822,0.72320056,-0.30985156,-0.07513308,0.16461043,-0.7699229,0.55152434,1.3765069,0.34521672,-1.5468284,-0.08093975,0.060523767,0.048074964,2.4866726,-0.77007675,-0.28912145,0.81280106,0.2360546,0.20183094,-0.12303582,0.3032121,0.9824135,-0.5324262,0.22713846,-0.8017688,1.8231386,0.32847893,-0.45982817,0.3885093,-0.008149003,0.3525789,-0.40070868,0.7522649,0.4164417,0.36903176,2.5783062,-1.6836613,1.90649,0.35491458,-0.38759676,0.308504,-0.21664496,0.7080224,0.78100467,0.6087256,2.6519156,0.6879251,-0.81678313,0.12348384,0.49592784,0.65658736,-0.8339956,0.01062985,0.23636188,-0.81746906,-1.3060066,-0.98607683,0.76358294,0.6982639,-0.91073936,-0.40032542,-0.47718903,0.73460156,0.22815938,0.21155758,-0.3318415,0.6559777,-0.41348457,-0.43594804,0.72237366,-0.49989212,-0.058945984,-0.56385964,-0.42154932,-1.2768722,-0.081511185,0.67775106,0.46615613,-0.06652979,-0.9099702,0.374312,-0.7951136,0.19289218,-0.58692664,-0.30924174,0.40086234,0.48675618,1.5349919,0.67708445,0.22086275,-0.97536236,-0.22947057,0.75645113,0.23976141,-0.5408452,-0.1290739,0.64246374,0.68889046,-0.758656,1.0016125,-0.84075195,0.45342216,0.