39	how can i create a new collation	To create a new collation in PostgreSQL 18, you can use the `CREATE COLLATION` command. Below is an example of how to create a collation using both built-in and ICU providers.\n\n### Using Builtin Provider\n\n```sql\nCREATE COLLATION my_custom_collation (provider = builtin, locale = 'en_US');\n```\n\n### Using ICU Provider\n\n```sql\nCREATE COLLATION my_icu_collation (provider = icu, locale = 'de_DE.UTF-8');\n```\n\nThese commands create a new collation with the specified locale and provider.	[0.3076639,-0.6008541,-3.6734748,-1.599571,0.72134084,-1.150055,-0.4959959,-0.18888023,-1.011167,-0.1688515,-1.0630649,0.20619461,1.7954779,0.8263961,0.1657969,-0.5451176,0.12072754,-0.9075721,-0.91622794,0.6926383,0.6183166,-1.6229471,1.3854778,-1.1557347,1.196289,-0.23537739,-0.09665175,0.61815244,-0.90121496,0.43521696,0.8273719,-0.0686621,-0.92843616,1.0705411,0.0002970129,-1.5022786,0.53421676,-0.1975729,-1.3440769,0.5895533,0.13333999,0.70784724,0.4628591,-1.1279482,0.769243,-0.79249185,1.4252203,-0.6444061,0.5564053,0.48105064,-0.6055509,1.1238527,0.16517682,-0.7147559,0.35857746,0.4857381,-0.542459,-0.18823223,0.26485413,-1.4721875,0.5624758,0.8283726,-0.07793932,0.85590774,0.80421317,-0.65022635,-0.92153454,1.1682844,-0.016137194,-0.70555985,-0.23384495,0.9661638,1.6257861,0.046072967,-1.1652039,-0.70356387,-0.03268478,0.1448814,0.1143503,0.15934011,0.914142,1.0424902,2.4317708,-1.4735595,1.6927617,-0.5799209,-0.034236003,0.2429293,-0.8147712,1.2362219,0.9355243,0.4006173,0.90266323,0.98491085,-0.4008429,0.21092248,-0.7934586,0.84398496,-0.5930662,-0.46709377,-0.6316083,0.18127707,0.87552625,-0.38527444,-0.5879034,0.31497493,0.16995274,-0.3763569,-1.202311,0.13557509,-1.0830264,-0.13940217,-0.608032,-0.10229198,0.48329043,-0.539132,0.8379898,-0.06667788,1.1121598,1.047371,-0.88910425,-0.9717167,-0.010922036,-0.06041249,-1.6399443,0.111989655,-0.057876788,0.41952905,1.0912757,-1.980326,-0.57511693,-0.4572204,-0.15927824,0.38967454,0.4