40	what is check_postgres ?	`check_postgres` is a tool for monitoring the health of your PostgreSQL database and reporting unusual conditions. It integrates with Nagios and MRTG but can also be run standalone.\n\nHere’s how you can use it:\n\n```bash\n# Example command to run check_postgres\ncheck_postgres --verbose\n```\n\nThis command will provide detailed output about the state of your PostgreSQL instance, helping you identify potential issues or optimize performance.	[0.82134056,1.1821702,-4.0357604,-0.22830966,1.2927848,-0.17115815,0.43746024,-0.3987678,-0.94371337,-0.37439993,0.8551037,0.9756605,0.31662518,-0.5757115,-0.7540473,-0.4860665,-0.16791289,-1.0884101,0.46206552,-0.3092057,-0.5343738,-1.1064688,-0.94438255,0.9496161,2.6598203,0.98292625,-0.46870127,0.14319484,-1.0817071,0.4286986,-0.6692394,0.7673389,-0.3949712,-1.2662156,-0.5227777,-1.6019518,0.36547104,0.7882055,-0.20916697,-0.45519716,-0.48075834,1.0970573,-0.37947595,-0.86068857,0.64746344,0.75062263,-0.09176086,-0.075910956,1.1547687,-1.4521072,-0.2547867,-0.29515973,0.6179367,0.6264467,1.1899813,0.70522,0.49392837,0.8014623,-0.41274142,-1.3313997,2.0840936,0.23875026,-0.15870073,1.1330138,0.22770317,-1.4003905,-0.28592032,-0.17111409,-0.3923301,-0.60366184,-0.33261245,0.10603835,0.6645032,0.24040285,0.5114182,0.021796733,-0.39474252,-0.69566715,0.8447232,-0.29387465,0.97591794,-0.1224166,1.609,0.31495115,0.2248662,-0.29199165,-0.6347505,-0.17102589,-1.2650992,1.2755805,0.2951867,-1.097313,0.26858512,0.47224465,-1.3555394,1.641099,0.26028118,-0.28005272,-1.048942,-0.17346837,-0.9000376,0.15798566,-0.14712045,-0.9324929,3.9301067e-05,0.31068268,-0.2297968,0.140372,-0.9450737,0.009882437,0.5370735,1.2852503,0.56253374,-0.96117496,0.20092711,0.6400627,1.5083998,-1.3201305,-0.19930854,0.3219166,-0.86312234,0.01696503,0.25332445,2.0830483,-1.8695066,-0.014692137,-0.4791073,0.68047553,-0.16798115,0.29029253,0.5427059,-0.8931793,-0.88061583,-0.046868395,0.45044988,1.5595967,0.76630867,-0.2004005,0.0559