41	how can i have the dead tuples number ?	To get the number of dead tuples, you can use the `pgstattuple` function or check the `dead_tuple_count` column from the output of `pgstattuple`. Here is how:\n\n```sql\nSELECT dead_tuple_count \nFROM pgstattuple('your_table_name');\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can view this information during a vacuum process using the `pg_stat_progress_vacuum` system view:\n\n```sql\nSELECT dead_tuple_bytes, num_dead_item_ids\nFROM pg_stat_progress_vacuum\nWHERE pid = pg_backend_pid();\n```\n\nThis will show you the amount of dead tuple data and the number of dead item identifiers collected during the current vacuum operation.	[-0.8661837,-0.8038595,-3.5388434,-1.7958103,0.81458163,0.28492334,0.70395476,0.99676657,-0.10728106,-0.6524077,-1.5021378,0.2748843,2.5251305,-0.99802303,-0.8542591,-1.1009434,1.3360304,-1.1208658,-0.38848183,0.38974902,0.08244554,-0.120713145,-0.91919184,-0.012636888,1.2613307,0.9273363,-0.04484735,1.5109843,-0.97407657,0.5581777,0.9559674,0.41315773,0.27277198,0.49485564,-0.3901104,-0.72069246,0.47820067,-0.092321075,1.2953155,0.88333297,0.1439007,-0.4120048,0.05980664,-0.11602086,0.49032852,-0.53437054,1.0557009,1.5746936,0.17916767,-0.8126944,0.3201771,-0.94643044,-0.077041075,-0.61774457,-0.1547774,-0.1464082,-0.681603,-1.0451046,0.9491883,0.42940858,0.121765144,1.2178403,-0.47473684,-0.21990825,1.288953,0.1339399,-0.5631956,0.4153799,-0.060492422,-0.39527437,0.03724889,0.91043997,0.597001,0.13805324,-0.4571493,0.5608348,-0.4049857,-0.22137594,0.34891975,0.6536054,-0.2674267,-0.079831064,2.5454338,-0.009408566,0.04045242,-0.24844863,-0.19693327,-1.2808233,-0.1833049,0.72855335,0.44372702,0.3166444,1.2684547,0.50313944,0.28210482,0.5808427,-0.08094828,0.7023818,-1.2253152,-1.294738,1.0200887,0.03219607,-0.520233,-1.3357301,-0.20360489,0.7013479,-0.24475633,-0.02790956,-0.030397857,0.7940498,-0.6821451,0.09404022,-0.95202094,-0.024480201,0.52943593,-0.12699367,0.4676694,-0.7695246,-0.77338266,0.38073254,-0.307325,