42	what parameters to set for effective vacuum ?	For effective vacuuming in PostgreSQL 18, consider setting these parameters:\n\n```sql\n# Set maintenance work memory higher if needed\nmaintenance_work_mem = '256MB'\n\n# Adjust autovacuum work memory based on workload\nautovacuum_work_mem = '64MB'  # or set it to -1 to use maintenance_work_mem\n\n# Enable cost-based vacuum delay for better concurrency\nvacuum_cost_delay = '1ms'\n```\n\nThese settings help balance performance and resource usage during vacuum operations. Adjust `maintenance_work_mem` based on your workload and available memory. Set `autovacuum_work_mem` to a reasonable value or use the default if not sure. Enable `cost-based vacuum delay` for better concurrent database activity handling.	[0.17215964,0.65251786,-3.756784,-0.65354824,1.2762239,1.0597897,-0.2779078,0.47461623,-1.2158066,1.2031718,-0.24543338,0.85206556,1.4539993,1.3242054,-0.14969501,0.07262929,0.8081746,-1.2918237,0.9500597,-0.71207875,-0.6801408,-1.0071898,-0.7120794,-1.4318293,1.3133018,1.0277898,1.1972154,1.5741692,0.54411054,-0.41732067,1.073349,0.49369234,-0.3566355,0.02244918,-0.66098094,-1.0235789,0.41483825,1.3826803,0.1437273,-0.48012146,-0.72341484,-1.0435541,0.46897873,-0.12826906,0.422087,0.9535338,0.25362727,-1.2725973,-0.08079675,-1.5075836,0.3459506,-2.3602238,-0.73911214,-0.6509339,1.4110677,0.6146729,-1.2556751,-0.09756795,1.1378996,-0.07612361,0.6760191,-0.023874218,-0.6171941,0.9243024,0.4706286,0.4323259,-0.57571995,0.4811965,-0.9984091,-1.1360693,0.44822827,-0.24244949,0.22555141,-1.0425056,-0.63081074,1.041846,-1.521035,-1.0608972,1.3318888,-0.39217883,-0.19832958,-0.013152433,1.5519904,-0.2692659,1.5724643,-1.0765086,-0.06841782,-0.22200453,-0.47682172,0.27590734,-0.041317698,0.20372891,-0.027252331,-0.15583408,0.5099347,0.8171732,-0.036242865,2.0006871,-0.22019163,-0.40155497,0.056997616,0.56415105,1.1432071,-0.49502033,-0.8358846,0.6914004,0.06010009,0.06524091,0.038556907,-0.8073767,-0.79242337,0.8967878,-0.395