44	how to set primary_conninfo parameter ?	To set the `primary_conninfo` parameter for a streaming replication setup, you need to configure it in either the `postgresql.conf` file or on the server command line during startup.\n\nHere is how you can do it:\n\n```ini\n# In postgresql.conf\nprimary_conninfo = 'host=192.168.1.50 port=5432 user=foo password=foopass options=""'\n```\n\nOr, on the server command line during startup:\n\n```sh\npostgres -c primary_conninfo='host=192.168.1.50 port=5432 user=foo password=foopass options=""'\n```\n\nMake sure to replace the placeholder values with your actual host, port, username, and password details.	[-0.4424053,-0.4379258,-3.1320763,-1.34823,0.5146941,-0.9954688,0.32527483,0.11810053,-1.1843585,-0.07555965,-0.66282284,0.6712561,1.6636914,0.7522826,0.96177965,-0.05325531,-0.36794987,-0.27989548,0.23214705,0.35822257,-0.44748113,-0.69339246,1.0001367,0.45959747,1.9119984,1.4871311,0.6453432,0.66470623,-0.52497315,0.5727064,-0.03431682,1.0152625,0.70715016,0.8563428,-0.8773839,-1.0139705,0.11541819,0.1649502,-0.80459356,1.0923842,-1.1172535,-0.33540437,0.45898286,-1.5452503,-0.3392512,-0.5191914,1.2660593,-0.07517288,1.219085,-0.59718424,-0.7877157,1.2639443,0.13354228,-1.7546539,0.33487058,0.5349206,0.089611284,1.5993358,1.3389391,-0.7219438,1.052727,0.30221674,-0.6284457,1.5222899,-0.24323173,-0.7614735,-1.0282323,0.6876797,-0.68257093,-0.71561974,-0.42769885,-0.5075258,-0.106724404,-0.21756451,0.70774525,-0.2148429,-0.560445,-0.8419865,0.12614514,0.4185677,0.14570914,0.36645386,1.7535586,-0.89948875,0.58363974,0.060433533,-0.7811897,-1.0104816,-0.36853933,0.3548696,0.34927544,0.8363528,-0.11433818,-0.3086412,-0.2792205,0.3942236,-0.9177719,0.8631862,1.3993934,-0.3236585,0.29741934,0.0050881193,-0.1386661,-0.18379301,-0.5906477,0.39995465,-0.030536225,-0.09893641,-0.019555414,-0.924227,-1.4225363,0.6904871,0.75028515,-0.3683586,0.809,-1.3642111,0.4151465,-0.57713825,1.0228482,0.6986189,-1.3849884,-1.0188576,1.5540562,2.542208