45	what are the possible values for wal_level parameter ?	The `wal_level` parameter can have the following values:\n\n```markdown\nreplica\nminimal\nlogical\n```\n\nEach value represents a different level of logging detail:\n\n- `replica`: Logs enough data to support replication and point-in-time recovery.\n- `minimal`: Logs only the information required for crash recovery and immediate shutdown, generating minimal WAL volume but not suitable for replication or point-in-time recovery.\n- `logical`: Adds information necessary for logical decoding, increasing the WAL volume.	[-0.33388945,0.9848995,-3.9132848,-1.2182282,0.8436943,0.268876,-0.22975992,-0.9230864,-0.7047056,0.3641621,-1.0801226,1.0539632,1.548506,0.9859917,0.15151414,-0.7991638,0.45300385,-0.96167284,0.94672805,-1.4040933,-0.43768093,-1.0137366,-0.57935244,-0.4174876,2.2622292,1.4562805,0.08967582,1.7224629,-0.9538923,0.078083426,0.17323817,-1.1871289,0.2055706,-0.4071779,-1.4444904,-0.73989767,1.1048392,0.31024945,0.05710291,0.42739326,-0.13455401,-0.8236316,1.0080394,0.84251225,0.04857041,0.82420516,0.364182,0.35317466,1.7316617,-1.3024602,-0.41139573,-0.55501235,-0.018543689,-0.19834879,1.4402686,0.44627637,-0.849139,0.4083398,0.6888246,0.15280123,1.1206639,0.61673,-0.84254104,0.6370152,0.12624218,-0.2561889,-0.9478371,0.28991905,-1.0057107,-1.3869864,1.1812412,0.41639253,-0.52206177,-1.2501448,-0.5420711,0.6995246,-0.34651995,-0.58497375,0.74023235,0.5318647,0.16083814,1.2143846,0.8261795,-0.042498443,0.42988932,-0.32810587,0.2579281,1.4205722,-0.618714,1.4525056,-0.31440642,0.43592978,0.44798627,-0.029618375,-1.1391082,0.3232725,0.012479002,1.4118849,-0.50007397,-0.7590663,-0.031544283,0.62989134,0.4303388,-0.03781328,0.28398618,1.5469799,0.07284611,-0.3895632,-0.9316686,0.033733156,-0.8911428,0.9959723,-0.7369642,-0.057609763,0.019525718,-1.0790157,1.478547,-0.38078392,0.33114752,0.9607556,0.063990906,-0.3551084,-0.44121662,0.49818122,0.6740309,-0.13658454,-0.6791698,0.310113,0.19575778,-0.7613674,