47	how do i use archive_command ?	To configure and use the `archive_command`, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Set Up the Archive Command**: Define a command that will copy archived WAL segments to an archive directory.\n\n2. **Enable Archival**: Set the `archive_mode` parameter to `on`.\n\n3. **Restart PostgreSQL**: Ensure PostgreSQL restarts for changes to take effect.\n\nHere is how you can do it:\n\n### Step 1: Configure `archive_command`\n\nEdit your `postgresql.conf` file and set the `archive_command`. For example, to use a simple shell command that copies files to an external directory:\n\n```markdown\narchive_mode = on\narchive_command = 'cp %p /path/to/archive/%f'\n```\n\n### Step 2: Enable Archival\n\nEnsure the `archive_mode` is enabled. This can be done in your `postgresql.conf` file:\n\n```markdown\narchive_mode = on\n```\n\n### Step 3: Restart PostgreSQL\n\nRestart PostgreSQL to apply the changes:\n\n```bash\nsudo systemctl restart postgresql\n```\n\nor if you are using a different init system:\n\n```bash\npg_ctl restart -D /path/to/data/directory\n```\n\nThis setup will enable WAL archiving according to the specified `archive_command`.	[-0.5959141,-0.6047284,-2.3996468,-1.6419464,0.9163462,-1.0814359,-1.067124,1.458513,-0.6857545,-0.018910777,-1.3994622,1.3726063,2.0916448,1.1336087,0.6320585,-0.10570894,-0.07281275,-0.22268927,0.28362694,0.5464803,1.0944263,-2.3681605,0.38892302,1.2424778,2.2175322,-0.032962482,0.34486407,1.6926048,-1.2032108,0.12732059,1.3152933,0.0129614575,-0.115360335,0.44136018,0.581092,-2.3659136,0.49209985,-1.5934756,-0.37757385,1.3124665,0.36262196,-0.040343266,-0.44874805,-0.14876257,0.21233201,0.65051764,0.013216898,0.32178468,1.0438242,-1.0842398,1.0620288,-0.90044385,-0.07691477,-0.043211628,0.86131126,0.02040044,0.22137769,-0.3590744,0.40357614,-1.9066324,0.51269084,-0.4397161,1.0402472,1.34493,1.3976781,1.3872035,-0.08415727,0.9817621,0.6803937,-1.0051811,1.1220895,-0.4470778,0.7531108,-1.512771,-0.31530452,0.2596433,-0.9289